althy.) We rolled checkout-api back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before trying to redeploy it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14310, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VNfGe33W4CqT59vsnUAkxY", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 14310, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VNfGe33W4CqT59vsnUAkxY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18337, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate. v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to it. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open and the on-call engineer has been paged. It describes the failure, the rollback and the result, and says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before anyone redeploys it.\n\nThe staging build of this release (v2.3.1-rc) was also marked unhealthy, so the problem was visible before the production deploy.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01P8XhbjVhEPV462ezU1s5Ur", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "nam